.\" Manual page for the mdn daemon, shipped in the md-notes Debian package
.\" (davison/md-notes#137). packaging/deb/build.sh substitutes @VERSION@ and
.\" @DATE@ at packaging time, so the footer names the release it shipped with.
.\"
.\" It exists because Debian Policy 12.1 asks every program in /usr/bin for
.\" one, and lintian says so; the alternative was a lintian override
.\" justifying its absence, and for a command with four subcommands the page
.\" is smaller than the justification.
.TH MDN 1 "@DATE@" "md-notes @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdn \- local markdown notes served to a browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdn
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdn
is a small local service that turns folders of markdown files into a notes
application in the browser, and doubles as a markdown viewer for any folder on
disk.
It renders notes server\-side, watches the configured roots for changes made by
other tools, searches them with
.BR rg (1),
and pushes changes to the open page over Server\-Sent Events.
.PP
It binds to localhost by default.
Notes stay plain markdown files in a folder hierarchy, editable with any tool
and synced by anything that syncs files.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the daemon against the configured notes root.
This is what the systemd user unit starts.
.TP
.BI "open " DIR
Register
.I DIR
with the running daemon and open it in the browser.
With
.B \-\-no\-browser
the URL is printed instead of opened.
.TP
.B token
Print the daemon's bearer token, which the browser extension needs.
.B \-\-rotate
replaces it with a new one.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mdn/config.yml
The daemon's configuration: the notes roots, the address to bind and the port.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/mdn.service
The systemd user unit this package installs.
Start it with
.RS
.PP
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now mdn
.fi
.RE
.SH DEPENDENCIES
The daemon shells out to
.BR rg (1)
to list and to search a root.
Without ripgrep the navigator is empty and search returns nothing, which is why
this package depends on it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rg (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
The full documentation is at
.UR https://github.com/davison/md-notes
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Darren Davison
